1
00:00:00,173 --> 00:00:02,940
(Scenes with child actors were filmed
safely with guardians and staff present.)

2
00:00:42,170 --> 00:00:45,112
I thought the world was being cruel
only to me.

3
00:00:53,015 --> 00:00:54,288
I resented it.

4
00:00:56,386 --> 00:00:57,724
I resented it over and over again.

5
00:01:01,461 --> 00:01:02,996
Even as time passed,

6
00:01:03,606 --> 00:01:05,866
the wound did not heal easily.

7
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:07,634
Mi Young.

8
00:01:10,978 --> 00:01:12,200
I really missed you.

9
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:14,942
I'm sorry,

10
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:17,742
but I would rather you didn't
acknowledge me from now on.

11
00:01:19,112 --> 00:01:20,246
As far as I'm concerned,

12
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:23,650
you no longer exist in this world.

13
00:01:25,774 --> 00:01:27,534
It's an unbelievable family drama...

14
00:01:28,331 --> 00:01:30,490
with the entire family tangled up in it.

15
00:01:31,958 --> 00:01:32,859
But...

16
00:01:33,507 --> 00:01:34,698
hidden inside that wound...

17
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:40,000
was a secret I knew nothing about.

18
00:01:42,589 --> 00:01:43,604
How?

19
00:01:46,889 --> 00:01:48,175
How could that be?

20
00:01:50,596 --> 00:01:51,445
Mi Young.

21
00:01:52,863 --> 00:01:53,780
Do you know...

22
00:01:55,409 --> 00:01:57,684
do you know how much I hated you
all this time?

23
00:01:58,585 --> 00:02:00,585
Then does that mean...

24
00:02:03,457 --> 00:02:05,492
the wound is no longer a wound?

25
00:02:07,977 --> 00:02:09,650
(Calvin)

26
00:02:12,332 --> 00:02:13,700
Yes, it's me.

27
00:02:17,119 --> 00:02:19,473
Now, I cannot be certain
of anything anymore.

28
00:02:20,212 --> 00:02:21,941
(Untitled)

29
00:02:21,942 --> 00:02:23,210
I cannot even be sure...

30
00:02:25,795 --> 00:02:27,047
of my own heart.

31
00:02:29,611 --> 00:02:31,404
(Episode 5)

32
00:02:32,111 --> 00:02:33,897
(This series is based on the novel
"Let's Get Divorced" by Kim Hyun Kyung.)

33
00:02:34,597 --> 00:02:36,424
(Written by Hwang Ji Eon)

34
00:02:37,217 --> 00:02:38,925
(Directed by Joo Sung Woo)

35
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:00,781
Wait.

36
00:03:01,358 --> 00:03:02,378
You've been working?

37
00:03:02,751 --> 00:03:05,152
What about you? Don't you have any plans
on your day off?

38
00:03:05,752 --> 00:03:08,488
The tennis club I go to is nearby.

39
00:03:09,423 --> 00:03:11,758
I was passing by and saw the door open,
so I thought I would stop in.

40
00:03:12,459 --> 00:03:14,695
But how do you work all the time
without ever taking a break?

41
00:03:15,395 --> 00:03:16,929
Come on. Let's go bowling together.

42
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:21,201
Kyung Tae.

43
00:03:24,447 --> 00:03:27,074
Say someone stabbed you in the back
really badly.

44
00:03:27,941 --> 00:03:28,942
What would you do?

45
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:30,944
Stabbed me in the back?

46
00:03:34,533 --> 00:03:37,684
Then I would have to get them back
the same way, I guess.

47
00:03:45,395 --> 00:03:46,293
Oh.

48
00:03:53,219 --> 00:03:54,601
Got you.

49
00:03:54,875 --> 00:03:56,035
Are you that happy?

50
00:03:56,375 --> 00:03:57,604
Of course.

51
00:03:57,848 --> 00:04:00,041
Do you know how many days I spent
trying to catch this?

52
00:04:01,141 --> 00:04:03,675
Anyway, thank you
for cooperating with the investigation.

53
00:04:11,318 --> 00:04:12,619
The painting is a little hard
to understand, right?

54
00:04:14,888 --> 00:04:17,066
No matter how many times I look at it,
I still don't really get it.

55
00:04:18,358 --> 00:04:19,139
What about you?

56
00:04:19,726 --> 00:04:21,193
I understood it at a glance.

57
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:22,362
Really?

58
00:04:24,498 --> 00:04:27,139
They certainly didn't hold back
on the paint.

59
00:04:27,591 --> 00:04:28,935
They used good brushes too.

60
00:04:30,064 --> 00:04:30,875
What?

61
00:04:35,404 --> 00:04:36,343
Look over there.

62
00:04:36,743 --> 00:04:38,378
What? No way.

63
00:04:38,379 --> 00:04:39,838
He's so handsome.

64
00:04:40,012 --> 00:04:41,248
He's coming this way.

65
00:04:54,027 --> 00:04:55,038
How was the exhibition?

66
00:04:55,492 --> 00:04:57,597
It was fun. I liked it.

67
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:01,550
Thank you. It's been a long time
since I came somewhere like this.

68
00:05:01,983 --> 00:05:02,936
You don't have to thank me.

69
00:05:03,596 --> 00:05:04,783
I should be thanking you.

70
00:05:05,056 --> 00:05:06,072
Thank you for coming with me.

71
00:05:15,441 --> 00:05:16,383
You haven't changed.

72
00:05:18,694 --> 00:05:19,986
The way your face looks when you smile...

73
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:21,288
is exactly the same.

74
00:05:22,221 --> 00:05:23,557
You look just like you did in college.

75
00:05:25,826 --> 00:05:28,228
What do you mean I haven't changed?
I've gotten old.

76
00:05:28,514 --> 00:05:29,763
Hey, old?

77
00:05:30,197 --> 00:05:32,100
If you say that around other people,
they will get mad at you.

78
00:05:32,374 --> 00:05:34,000
No, stop it.

79
00:05:34,267 --> 00:05:35,936
What? I'm serious.

80
00:05:36,703 --> 00:05:38,972
Should I ask the people here?

81
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:40,974
Excuse me.

82
00:05:41,835 --> 00:05:42,809
Okay.

83
00:05:43,222 --> 00:05:44,544
I haven't gotten old.

84
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,415
That's nice.

85
00:05:50,283 --> 00:05:51,384
The way you smile.

86
00:05:51,867 --> 00:05:53,019
I like seeing you smile.

87
00:05:57,947 --> 00:05:58,792
Do you think...

88
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:02,629
you could spare a little more time?

89
00:06:05,799 --> 00:06:07,799
There is somewhere I want to go with you.

90
00:06:16,705 --> 00:06:18,678
This place hasn't changed at all.

91
00:06:22,883 --> 00:06:24,384
Even this sofa is still the same.

92
00:06:25,685 --> 00:06:26,953
This spot right here...

93
00:06:27,123 --> 00:06:28,889
used to be our usual seat.

94
00:06:33,793 --> 00:06:35,295
It's here.

95
00:06:37,834 --> 00:06:38,665
Do you remember?

96
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:40,934
We stayed up all night here together...

97
00:06:41,301 --> 00:06:42,936
because we wanted to finish this
in one day.

98
00:06:45,939 --> 00:06:48,138
We both loved it back then.

99
00:06:51,839 --> 00:06:52,646
The comics, I mean.

100
00:06:55,715 --> 00:06:57,810
So what should we read today?

101
00:07:08,215 --> 00:07:09,229
You want to read this one?

102
00:07:09,735 --> 00:07:10,363
Here.

103
00:07:16,903 --> 00:07:17,706
A debt?

104
00:07:17,818 --> 00:07:19,698
Your hair got pulled out pretty badly...

105
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:21,374
by my mom last time.

106
00:07:23,743 --> 00:07:26,212
Oh, that?

107
00:07:26,799 --> 00:07:27,747
It's fine.

108
00:07:28,748 --> 00:07:30,706
I pulled out just as much of hers.

109
00:07:30,819 --> 00:07:32,313
Oh, I see.

110
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,893
Do you always investigate like this?
To catch people having affairs?

111
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:38,227
Well, I have to.

112
00:07:39,147 --> 00:07:41,353
Calling this legal work makes it
sound nice. It's basically hard labor.

113
00:07:41,828 --> 00:07:45,031
I thought people with professional titles
had easier lives.

114
00:07:45,341 --> 00:07:47,341
My life used to be a little easier.

115
00:07:48,568 --> 00:07:50,937
But a year ago, I got bitten by a python.

116
00:07:52,228 --> 00:07:53,173
Now,

117
00:07:53,408 --> 00:07:55,602
I don't even have an office, so I spend
all my time running around in the field.

118
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:57,077
A python?

119
00:07:57,777 --> 00:07:58,745
There is one.

120
00:07:59,846 --> 00:08:01,047
A 200-year-old python...

121
00:08:01,682 --> 00:08:03,016
who lives in Sinwol-dong.

122
00:08:10,613 --> 00:08:13,626
Anyway, it must be really tough
not even having an office.

123
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:17,897
If it were nothing but hard work,
I couldn't keep doing this.

124
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:20,604
When I work hard and win a case,

125
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:22,291
the money is pretty good.

126
00:08:22,437 --> 00:08:24,938
Oh, so the money is pretty good.

127
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:33,780
Yes. This is Jeon Chi Hyun.

128
00:08:34,047 --> 00:08:37,150
I'm the attorney representing Ji Won Ho.

129
00:08:37,617 --> 00:08:38,485
Oh, yes.

130
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:40,186
I sent you our response,

131
00:08:40,187 --> 00:08:42,187
so please check it
through the e-litigation system.

132
00:08:42,793 --> 00:08:43,723
Goodbye.

133
00:08:44,257 --> 00:08:45,424
What was that?

134
00:08:45,959 --> 00:08:47,727
Why was he so unpleasant?

135
00:08:49,696 --> 00:08:50,898
"A divorce claim."

136
00:08:56,224 --> 00:08:57,704
Come on!

137
00:09:06,842 --> 00:09:08,348
It's been such a long time...

138
00:09:08,748 --> 00:09:10,150
since we walked together like this.

139
00:09:12,118 --> 00:09:13,019
It really has.

140
00:09:14,098 --> 00:09:16,156
I thought we would never have
a day like this again.

141
00:09:18,024 --> 00:09:19,059
I'm really happy.

142
00:09:21,661 --> 00:09:22,495
I wish...

143
00:09:25,554 --> 00:09:28,201
we could just stay like this.

144
00:09:29,581 --> 00:09:31,204
We could work together comfortably...

145
00:09:32,806 --> 00:09:35,141
and talk over tea once in a while.

146
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:37,811
Okay.

147
00:09:38,668 --> 00:09:39,946
I won't ask for anything more.

148
00:09:41,101 --> 00:09:42,048
And...

149
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,259
I'm getting divorced soon.

150
00:09:50,523 --> 00:09:51,424
Mi Young.

151
00:09:51,858 --> 00:09:53,960
The reason I'm telling you this...

152
00:09:55,562 --> 00:09:57,263
is because I want to make
one thing perfectly clear.

153
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,299
Regardless of my situation,

154
00:09:59,955 --> 00:10:01,701
there can never be anything
between us again.

155
00:10:06,906 --> 00:10:07,774
Just a second.

156
00:10:10,845 --> 00:10:12,145
Yes, ma'am.

157
00:10:12,412 --> 00:10:14,514
I just received their response.

158
00:10:14,914 --> 00:10:15,748
Oh, okay.

159
00:10:16,022 --> 00:10:17,005
I'll send you screenshots...

160
00:10:17,292 --> 00:10:19,586
of the response by text.
Please check them right away.

161
00:10:20,019 --> 00:10:20,883
Okay.

162
00:10:27,303 --> 00:10:30,483
(The defendant states
that he has no intention of divorcing.)

163
00:10:43,086 --> 00:10:43,946
What is this?

164
00:10:44,811 --> 00:10:45,712
It's a response.

165
00:10:45,905 --> 00:10:47,547
Yes, I'm asking what this is!

166
00:10:47,912 --> 00:10:49,983
Why are you suddenly saying
you won't get divorced?

167
00:10:49,984 --> 00:10:51,484
What got into you?

168
00:10:52,185 --> 00:10:53,546
I just changed my mind.

169
00:10:54,038 --> 00:10:54,787
What?

170
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:57,423
Do you want me to say it again?

171
00:11:01,794 --> 00:11:02,962
I am not...

172
00:11:04,794 --> 00:11:05,688
divorcing you.

173
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:09,636
That must have been
a wake-up call for her.

174
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:11,571
All of a sudden,
he doesn't want a divorce.

175
00:11:12,134 --> 00:11:13,808
A man who was coming out...

176
00:11:13,888 --> 00:11:17,010
of a motel with another woman
just a few days ago?

177
00:11:17,255 --> 00:11:19,746
She must be wondering what is going on.

178
00:11:19,788 --> 00:11:21,080
Just wait.

179
00:11:21,248 --> 00:11:23,082
Now they are the ones who will be anxious.

180
00:11:24,553 --> 00:11:25,251
Right.

181
00:11:26,019 --> 00:11:28,588
Could you please stop
bringing up the motel now?

182
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:31,658
You can never be too careful
when it comes to playing with fire.

183
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:34,561
I'm not the one playing with fire. She is!

184
00:11:35,999 --> 00:11:38,164
I never thought my wife would
do something like that.

185
00:11:39,265 --> 00:11:40,567
I was too naive.

186
00:11:45,838 --> 00:11:47,674
Do you think you can
really go through with this?

187
00:11:48,041 --> 00:11:48,741
What?

188
00:11:49,075 --> 00:11:51,678
Your eyes are still full
of lingering feelings.

189
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:54,747
You're not ready yet.

190
00:11:55,648 --> 00:11:56,916
You're not ready to let her go.

191
00:11:58,918 --> 00:11:59,819
You mean it looks like...

192
00:12:01,054 --> 00:12:04,023
I have not completely moved on yet?

193
00:12:04,290 --> 00:12:05,525
Not at all.

194
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:12,281
Anyway, I refuse to let my wife
stab me in the back again.

195
00:12:12,832 --> 00:12:15,201
I'm going to win this lawsuit.
No matter what.

196
00:12:15,301 --> 00:12:18,004
That's exactly why
we're using this strategy.

197
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:19,292
But...

198
00:12:20,212 --> 00:12:22,442
she can never find out what we are doing.

199
00:12:23,732 --> 00:12:25,945
She must never find out...

200
00:12:25,985 --> 00:12:29,270
that saying you don't want a divorce was
nothing more than a strategy...

201
00:12:29,564 --> 00:12:31,385
and not your true intention.

202
00:12:32,151 --> 00:12:33,998
Then what am I supposed to do?

203
00:12:35,378 --> 00:12:36,456
You have to go back in.

204
00:12:37,785 --> 00:12:38,858
Go back where?

205
00:12:39,265 --> 00:12:42,428
To the place where you feel
the most uncomfortable...

206
00:12:43,418 --> 00:12:44,364
and can barely stand to be.

207
00:12:45,257 --> 00:12:46,332
We absolutely...

208
00:12:46,933 --> 00:12:48,368
have to win this lawsuit.

209
00:12:56,009 --> 00:13:00,035
Look at this.
There is not a single unnecessary word.

210
00:13:01,774 --> 00:13:03,449
There is a technical term for this.

211
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:05,652
It's called a backstab.

212
00:13:07,202 --> 00:13:08,221
We can't stay still.

213
00:13:09,188 --> 00:13:12,091
I need to prepare
an even stronger written brief.

214
00:13:12,495 --> 00:13:15,395
But why would he suddenly say
he doesn't want a divorce?

215
00:13:16,029 --> 00:13:18,495
Could he have changed his mind already?

216
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:22,368
Why? Why would he suddenly do that?

217
00:13:22,669 --> 00:13:26,862
This must all be a trick
by that 200-year-old python...

218
00:13:33,409 --> 00:13:34,580
I mean, a strategy.

219
00:13:35,415 --> 00:13:37,183
A strategy to shake us up mentally.

220
00:13:37,617 --> 00:13:39,215
Shake us up mentally?

221
00:13:41,788 --> 00:13:43,656
If one side keeps holding out,

222
00:13:43,961 --> 00:13:46,793
the side with less patience will
eventually give in.

223
00:13:47,093 --> 00:13:48,613
He's hoping you will get so exhausted...

224
00:13:48,614 --> 00:13:50,997
that you give up on everything
and just beg him for the divorce.

225
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:55,101
Then he will probably try to lowball you
on the property settlement too.

226
00:13:56,126 --> 00:13:57,704
And he will certainly go after control
of the company.

227
00:14:00,306 --> 00:14:02,885
There is really nothing complicated
about the strategy.

228
00:14:02,886 --> 00:14:05,278
He will simply keep holding out...

229
00:14:05,598 --> 00:14:08,047
until you get exhausted and give in first.

230
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:09,431
So, that's what he's doing.

231
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:11,651
Don't worry.

232
00:14:12,085 --> 00:14:14,821
We just have to hit him back even harder.

233
00:14:15,922 --> 00:14:16,989
But from now on,

234
00:14:17,657 --> 00:14:20,063
you cannot let your guard down
for even a second.

235
00:14:23,563 --> 00:14:24,530
What if...

236
00:14:25,398 --> 00:14:26,966
he actually means it?

237
00:14:27,667 --> 00:14:28,735
I mean,

238
00:14:30,069 --> 00:14:33,473
it could be sincere, not just a strategy.

239
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,475
So you're saying...

240
00:14:36,172 --> 00:14:39,879
there is a chance
Ji Won Ho really does not want a divorce?

241
00:14:40,112 --> 00:14:42,248
Of course there is.

242
00:14:43,383 --> 00:14:46,853
You were the one
who filed for divorce first,

243
00:14:47,176 --> 00:14:50,670
and Won Ho has basically been
dragged along with whatever you wanted.

244
00:14:50,763 --> 00:14:52,325
Dragged along? Who?

245
00:14:52,326 --> 00:14:53,993
He always does whatever he wants.

246
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,028
With Won Ho's personality,

247
00:14:56,029 --> 00:14:59,399
if he really wanted a divorce,
he would have done it already.

248
00:15:00,556 --> 00:15:02,467
If you think about it,

249
00:15:02,989 --> 00:15:06,606
he was the one who kept
putting off the divorce...

250
00:15:07,209 --> 00:15:08,274
using work as an excuse.

251
00:15:08,396 --> 00:15:09,842
Would a man who doesn't want a divorce...

252
00:15:09,976 --> 00:15:12,245
move out and live in a motel
before the divorce is even finalized?

253
00:15:12,416 --> 00:15:14,881
And as if that weren't enough,
bring another woman there too?

254
00:15:14,916 --> 00:15:16,615
He brought a woman there?

255
00:15:17,622 --> 00:15:19,262
Who? When?

256
00:15:19,416 --> 00:15:20,420
Someone.

257
00:15:20,649 --> 00:15:22,449
Are you sure it was a motel?
And are you sure it was a woman?

258
00:15:22,596 --> 00:15:24,991
Yes. I told you, I saw them.

259
00:15:32,634 --> 00:15:33,933
No way. I got goosebumps.

260
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:36,169
You really sent the response like that?

261
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:38,331
You're really preparing for a fight.

262
00:15:38,638 --> 00:15:41,641
Yes. After hearing what my lawyer said,
I thought that'd be the better approach.

263
00:15:46,412 --> 00:15:49,048
Mi Young must be completely stunned
by now.

264
00:15:49,749 --> 00:15:52,316
That response was the first time
you told her you weren't getting divorced.

265
00:15:53,986 --> 00:15:55,321
Even without any warning!

266
00:15:55,376 --> 00:15:56,722
Hey, if we're keeping score,

267
00:15:56,723 --> 00:15:59,592
do you know how many bombshells
Baek Mi Young has dropped on me?

268
00:15:59,937 --> 00:16:02,683
She needs to know what it feels like
to be blindsided too.

269
00:16:03,457 --> 00:16:06,257
But what are you really going to do
about Mi Young from now on?

270
00:16:06,839 --> 00:16:08,367
What do you mean, what am I going to do?

271
00:16:08,683 --> 00:16:09,635
With things this tense between you two,

272
00:16:10,203 --> 00:16:11,997
do you really think you can
keep working together?

273
00:16:12,505 --> 00:16:15,441
That's for her to decide.
I can't be the one to leave.

274
00:16:18,110 --> 00:16:19,111
And...

275
00:16:19,773 --> 00:16:21,247
I'm moving back in now.

276
00:16:21,573 --> 00:16:22,348
Moving back in?

277
00:16:23,059 --> 00:16:23,753
Where?

278
00:16:24,217 --> 00:16:26,217
The code name for this operation is...

279
00:16:27,253 --> 00:16:28,721
"Sleeping with the Enemy."

280
00:16:39,388 --> 00:16:40,900
He's hoping you will get so exhausted...

281
00:16:40,901 --> 00:16:43,169
that you give up on everything
and just beg him for the divorce.

282
00:16:43,487 --> 00:16:46,639
Then he will probably try to lowball you
on the property settlement too.

283
00:16:47,173 --> 00:16:48,741
And he will certainly go after control
of the company.

284
00:16:49,809 --> 00:16:52,078
Surely he wouldn't go that far.

285
00:16:53,045 --> 00:16:54,347
Do you want me to say it again?

286
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:57,483
I am not divorcing you.

287
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:00,953
This crazy...

288
00:17:03,671 --> 00:17:04,624
Ji Won Ho.

289
00:17:04,991 --> 00:17:07,393
So this is how low you're going to stoop?

290
00:17:15,976 --> 00:17:17,036
Why is this not working?

291
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:28,414
What?

292
00:17:29,248 --> 00:17:30,580
Did you change the passcode?

293
00:17:31,350 --> 00:17:32,320
What's this?

294
00:17:32,467 --> 00:17:34,467
Why did you change the passcode?

295
00:17:41,658 --> 00:17:43,663
What are you doing here?

296
00:17:43,845 --> 00:17:45,952
What do you mean?
Do I need your permission to come home?

297
00:17:47,145 --> 00:17:49,068
What are you doing? Open the door.

298
00:17:50,937 --> 00:17:52,972
Open it now.

299
00:18:02,536 --> 00:18:04,463
What are you doing?

300
00:18:04,464 --> 00:18:06,686
Did you really come back?

301
00:18:08,049 --> 00:18:08,876
Hey.

302
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:11,257
Do you really not want to get divorced?

303
00:18:11,549 --> 00:18:13,025
Hey, Ji Won Ho!

304
00:18:20,403 --> 00:18:22,403
This is crazy. Absolutely crazy.

305
00:18:23,049 --> 00:18:25,616
Mr. Ji came home
in the middle of the night?

306
00:18:26,038 --> 00:18:27,206
Yes.

307
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,308
What did he say?

308
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:32,053
Did he say he wants
to work things out with you again?

309
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:34,413
Then why?

310
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:36,206
Why did he suddenly come back?

311
00:18:36,616 --> 00:18:38,616
He just said it was his house,
so he came home.

312
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:39,919
Right.

313
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:42,288
He's not exactly wrong about that.

314
00:18:42,993 --> 00:18:44,590
But...

315
00:18:44,991 --> 00:18:46,726
if you're really getting divorced,

316
00:18:47,246 --> 00:18:49,629
isn't that going to be incredibly awkward?

317
00:18:49,746 --> 00:18:50,896
Exactly.

318
00:18:51,133 --> 00:18:53,399
Now we're going to be around each other
24 hours a day.

319
00:18:53,593 --> 00:18:56,033
How did I live with Ji Won Ho
for seven years?

320
00:18:58,371 --> 00:19:00,573
This really is "Sleeping with the Enemy."

321
00:19:02,074 --> 00:19:03,909
It must have been
incredibly awkward last night.

322
00:19:05,011 --> 00:19:06,202
You didn't get any sleep, did you?

323
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:08,422
Why would I not sleep?

324
00:19:08,423 --> 00:19:09,682
We already slept in separate rooms anyway.

325
00:19:10,068 --> 00:19:10,850
That's true.

326
00:19:11,584 --> 00:19:14,100
You two have always been used to feeling
uncomfortable around each other.

327
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:16,322
Well, if you put it like that.

328
00:19:16,673 --> 00:19:17,923
Anyway, be careful.

329
00:19:18,257 --> 00:19:19,892
If you let your guard down
in this situation,

330
00:19:19,893 --> 00:19:21,427
you could end up taking a serious hit too.

331
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:22,662
I know.

332
00:19:24,173 --> 00:19:26,173
I'll be careful not to play with fire.
Very careful.

333
00:19:32,047 --> 00:19:34,807
Mr. Ji, I have something to tell you.

334
00:19:35,207 --> 00:19:37,207
Can I see you for a little while today?

335
00:19:37,801 --> 00:19:39,078
Gosh.

336
00:19:39,979 --> 00:19:41,979
Now how am I supposed
to put out this fire?

337
00:19:42,885 --> 00:19:43,649
Fire?

338
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:46,525
There is one.
The little matchstick from Milan.

339
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:49,455
I'm an orphan now.

340
00:19:51,123 --> 00:19:53,426
An orphan? What do you mean?

341
00:19:53,826 --> 00:19:56,962
My father told me
never to contact him again.

342
00:19:57,997 --> 00:20:00,199
He told me not to look for him
for the rest of his life.

343
00:20:00,372 --> 00:20:01,940
Why?

344
00:20:03,602 --> 00:20:05,171
I reached out to him recently...

345
00:20:05,504 --> 00:20:08,040
because it was the anniversary
of my mom's passing.

346
00:20:08,774 --> 00:20:11,043
And apparently,
they got into a huge fight over it.

347
00:20:12,546 --> 00:20:15,347
He told me he never wants
any more trouble because of me.

348
00:20:28,394 --> 00:20:29,283
Are you okay?

349
00:20:30,723 --> 00:20:31,997
Of course I'm not.

350
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:36,402
I'm so sorry.

351
00:20:40,306 --> 00:20:41,061
Would you...

352
00:20:42,435 --> 00:20:44,243
be willing to be friends with me?

353
00:20:45,163 --> 00:20:45,978
Friends?

354
00:20:46,499 --> 00:20:51,016
I don't have anyone in my life
I can have deep conversations with.

355
00:20:51,686 --> 00:20:54,286
I just want to grab a drink
with you sometimes...

356
00:20:54,479 --> 00:20:56,622
and talk about what's really on my mind.

357
00:20:57,690 --> 00:20:59,525
Having just that would keep me going.

358
00:21:06,398 --> 00:21:07,666
Then promise me one thing.

359
00:21:10,136 --> 00:21:13,372
Never say you have feelings for me
or anything like that again.

360
00:21:13,539 --> 00:21:16,008
And let's make sure
we never cross the line as friends.

361
00:21:19,461 --> 00:21:20,446
Okay.

362
00:21:21,147 --> 00:21:22,615
You haven't eaten yet, right?

363
00:21:22,888 --> 00:21:24,283
Let's go grab a bite.

364
00:21:33,819 --> 00:21:34,927
This is delicious.

365
00:21:34,986 --> 00:21:36,592
Right up my alley.

366
00:21:38,112 --> 00:21:38,931
Really?

367
00:21:39,778 --> 00:21:40,912
What's your type, then?

368
00:21:50,490 --> 00:21:53,245
It's way too spicy.

369
00:22:07,609 --> 00:22:08,627
You finish it.

370
00:22:21,907 --> 00:22:23,475
You do it too.

371
00:22:24,907 --> 00:22:27,207
Why are we even doing this?

372
00:22:27,341 --> 00:22:28,702
Look into my eyes for three seconds.

373
00:22:28,727 --> 00:22:30,182
One, two, three... okay, that's enough.

374
00:22:30,716 --> 00:22:32,017
Let's stop.

375
00:22:32,083 --> 00:22:34,553
- Come on.
- Your hat fell off.

376
00:22:37,323 --> 00:22:39,024
Let's go around one more time.

377
00:22:45,350 --> 00:22:47,066
One, two, three.

378
00:22:50,187 --> 00:22:51,504
One, two, three.

379
00:23:12,045 --> 00:23:13,525
Won Ho, time to call it a day.

380
00:23:13,552 --> 00:23:15,461
I'm heading out. See you tomorrow.

381
00:23:27,673 --> 00:23:29,942
What made you call me out this time?

382
00:23:30,209 --> 00:23:31,010
Well,

383
00:23:31,844 --> 00:23:33,178
nothing in particular.

384
00:23:33,679 --> 00:23:34,446
What?

385
00:23:34,886 --> 00:23:36,615
We're friends, aren't we?

386
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:39,046
Friends can hang out...

387
00:23:39,219 --> 00:23:41,650
and have a drink
without overthinking things.

388
00:23:43,489 --> 00:23:45,824
I can never win an argument with you.

389
00:23:47,426 --> 00:23:48,693
Then how about...

390
00:23:49,361 --> 00:23:51,096
trying to outdrink me tonight?

391
00:23:52,811 --> 00:23:53,732
What do you say?

392
00:23:54,133 --> 00:23:55,199
Loser...

393
00:23:56,519 --> 00:23:57,736
covers the tab.

394
00:24:02,857 --> 00:24:03,676
Deal.

395
00:24:06,443 --> 00:24:07,280
Wait.

396
00:24:07,506 --> 00:24:08,614
Oh, come on.

397
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:15,612
Let's go for round two.

398
00:24:15,613 --> 00:24:17,656
Drink any more,
and you're going to pass out.

399
00:24:17,786 --> 00:24:19,558
Who's passing out? Nonsense.

400
00:24:19,916 --> 00:24:22,161
Mr. Ji, this is your place, right?

401
00:24:22,319 --> 00:24:23,673
Yes, it is.

402
00:24:23,674 --> 00:24:24,763
This is my house.

403
00:24:24,964 --> 00:24:26,565
Hold on.

404
00:24:27,626 --> 00:24:29,368
The passcode...

405
00:24:47,402 --> 00:24:48,490
Mr. Ji.

406
00:24:48,491 --> 00:24:51,317
Let's have a drink inside too.

407
00:24:51,464 --> 00:24:52,825
Let's drink.

408
00:24:53,257 --> 00:24:55,257
All of us...

409
00:24:56,996 --> 00:24:59,331
My back is killing me.

410
00:24:59,794 --> 00:25:00,833
It hurts.

411
00:25:03,301 --> 00:25:05,137
Hey, Ji Won Ho.

412
00:25:05,234 --> 00:25:06,720
Have you lost your mind?

413
00:25:06,721 --> 00:25:08,340
Can I get some water?

414
00:25:08,528 --> 00:25:10,534
Please, get me some water.

415
00:25:15,649 --> 00:25:18,417
In all my life,
I've never seen anything like this.

416
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:20,586
I mean, a motel is one thing.

417
00:25:20,853 --> 00:25:23,288
Bringing another woman
straight into our home?

418
00:25:23,555 --> 00:25:25,157
Isn't this insane?

419
00:25:25,234 --> 00:25:26,258
Unbelievable...

420
00:25:26,771 --> 00:25:29,128
This isn't some trashy soap opera.

421
00:25:29,378 --> 00:25:32,031
The look that woman gave me...

422
00:25:33,536 --> 00:25:35,902
Just thinking about it
makes my blood boil.

423
00:25:37,736 --> 00:25:39,438
I'm not overreacting, am I?

424
00:25:39,576 --> 00:25:41,576
Not at all.

425
00:25:42,107 --> 00:25:45,296
Then let's channel that anger...

426
00:25:45,297 --> 00:25:47,212
and start drafting the petition right now.

427
00:25:50,682 --> 00:25:53,218
Let's start from the beginning.
It'll help...

428
00:25:53,285 --> 00:25:56,488
if we capture just how furious you were
in more vivid detail.

429
00:25:56,662 --> 00:25:57,890
So,

430
00:25:58,223 --> 00:26:01,969
the two of them practically
barged through the door together,

431
00:26:01,994 --> 00:26:03,395
all over each other.

432
00:26:04,263 --> 00:26:07,666
Then that woman gave me this bizarre look,

433
00:26:07,667 --> 00:26:10,269
while Ji Won Ho grabbed my pant leg,
begging for water.

434
00:26:10,803 --> 00:26:12,137
And that wasn't even the worst of it.

435
00:26:12,215 --> 00:26:13,806
You remember my mother-in-law, right?

436
00:26:14,106 --> 00:26:16,208
When we visited her house that time...

437
00:26:17,109 --> 00:26:20,212
Are you really going to cook
my birthday meal yourself?

438
00:26:20,287 --> 00:26:22,347
Mi Young, I'll help you out today.

439
00:26:23,515 --> 00:26:26,108
Your back is bad.
Why are you on your feet doing chores?

440
00:26:26,133 --> 00:26:27,453
Go lie down.

441
00:26:28,047 --> 00:26:29,788
Have you given up on having a baby?

442
00:26:30,093 --> 00:26:30,647
Excuse me?

443
00:26:30,707 --> 00:26:33,392
You're not throwing in the towel
just because it failed once, are you?

444
00:26:33,925 --> 00:26:36,148
I can only imagine how brilliant
and gorgeous a grandchild would be...

445
00:26:36,173 --> 00:26:37,362
taking after Won Ho.

446
00:26:37,596 --> 00:26:41,233
The Defendant's mother severely
mistreated the Plaintiff,

447
00:26:41,500 --> 00:26:43,601
subjecting her to excessive interference,
contempt, and verbal insults.

448
00:26:43,626 --> 00:26:45,070
(Pleading)

449
00:26:45,204 --> 00:26:47,539
I feel sorry for how your life turned out.

450
00:26:47,973 --> 00:26:49,834
You don't even have
parents-in-law to lean on.

451
00:26:50,020 --> 00:26:52,544
How could both of them pass away so
before their time?

452
00:26:52,753 --> 00:26:55,760
The Defendant's mother opposed
the marriage from the outset...

453
00:26:55,881 --> 00:26:57,416
Did you say that, Mi Young?

454
00:26:57,583 --> 00:26:59,960
Did you tell her you can't have a baby
because I'm stressing you out?

455
00:26:59,985 --> 00:27:00,433
What?

456
00:27:00,473 --> 00:27:01,553
Throughout the marriage,

457
00:27:01,700 --> 00:27:03,152
she belittled the Plaintiff's family...

458
00:27:03,176 --> 00:27:04,957
and subjected her
to constant verbal abuse.

459
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:08,927
You try so hard to be nice
that Mom thinks she can walk all over you.

460
00:27:09,330 --> 00:27:11,330
We shouldn't have come. I told you not to.

461
00:27:11,390 --> 00:27:13,390
You have no problem talking back to me.

462
00:27:13,597 --> 00:27:15,100
Yet the Defendant consistently...

463
00:27:15,457 --> 00:27:19,171
turned a blind eye and stood idly by.

464
00:27:19,284 --> 00:27:21,284
No, I'm never changing it.

465
00:27:21,484 --> 00:27:23,604
Unless Man Joo asks me to, I won't budge.

466
00:27:23,605 --> 00:27:24,776
Furthermore,

467
00:27:24,904 --> 00:27:26,787
the Defendant
never treated the Plaintiff...

468
00:27:26,812 --> 00:27:29,548
as anything more than a business partner,

469
00:27:30,349 --> 00:27:33,919
and even when the Plaintiff was ill
and required frequent hospital visits,

470
00:27:34,067 --> 00:27:37,289
she received no care or consideration
from the Defendant.

471
00:27:37,856 --> 00:27:39,860
Such was the extent
of the Defendant's indifference...

472
00:27:39,885 --> 00:27:41,827
toward the Plaintiff
throughout their marriage.

473
00:27:42,928 --> 00:27:47,132
The Defendant displayed severe mood swings
and apparent anger management issues,

474
00:27:47,492 --> 00:27:49,773
and whenever he failed
to regulate his emotions,

475
00:27:49,798 --> 00:27:53,372
he subjected the Plaintiff to both direct
and indirect physical violence.

476
00:27:54,865 --> 00:27:57,576
Consequently, the Plaintiff sought
psychiatric treatment...

477
00:27:58,610 --> 00:28:00,913
and was diagnosed with panic disorder.

478
00:28:04,024 --> 00:28:06,952
The marriage ultimately
collapsed due to...

479
00:28:07,753 --> 00:28:09,555
an act of physical assault.

480
00:28:11,657 --> 00:28:15,727
The Defendant inflicted
severe bodily bruising on the Plaintiff,

481
00:28:16,995 --> 00:28:18,697
after which the Plaintiff and Defendant...

482
00:28:19,198 --> 00:28:21,667
began sleeping in separate rooms.

483
00:28:23,402 --> 00:28:25,372
The Plaintiff made repeated attempts...

484
00:28:25,409 --> 00:28:27,443
to resolve their conflict amicably
through conversation,

485
00:28:27,695 --> 00:28:29,508
which the Defendant persistently avoided,

486
00:28:30,042 --> 00:28:33,045
and despite the de facto breakdown
of the marital relationship,

487
00:28:33,478 --> 00:28:37,115
the Plaintiff continued to maintain
the household and business...

488
00:28:37,616 --> 00:28:39,151
out of a lingering sense of attachment.

489
00:28:47,784 --> 00:28:50,095
That's amazing. Really?

490
00:28:51,457 --> 00:28:53,799
You went all the way out there
just for photos?

491
00:28:54,700 --> 00:28:56,935
I know, right? The view is breathtaking.

492
00:28:58,253 --> 00:28:59,571
Sounds like you had a blast.

493
00:28:59,833 --> 00:29:01,573
All right, see you at the office tomorrow.

494
00:29:01,746 --> 00:29:02,447
Bye.

495
00:29:03,726 --> 00:29:04,549
Hey.

496
00:29:05,644 --> 00:29:06,945
Turn the volume down.

497
00:29:07,379 --> 00:29:09,615
I can't sleep over your game.

498
00:29:09,948 --> 00:29:12,473
Are you serious?
Your voice is louder than the game.

499
00:29:12,474 --> 00:29:14,693
The neighbors are going to complain again.

500
00:29:14,694 --> 00:29:15,454
What?

501
00:29:15,954 --> 00:29:17,623
Step outside.

502
00:29:17,889 --> 00:29:18,857
Let's talk outside.

503
00:29:20,559 --> 00:29:22,471
Fine by me. Let's take it out there.

504
00:29:22,472 --> 00:29:24,062
You think I'm going to back down?

505
00:29:30,769 --> 00:29:33,438
Is this why you came in here?

506
00:29:33,536 --> 00:29:36,181
What did I do this time?

507
00:29:36,182 --> 00:29:39,434
You were blatantly flirting and giggling
with that young kid, weren't you?

508
00:29:39,435 --> 00:29:40,279
Are you out of your mind?

509
00:29:40,280 --> 00:29:42,881
You're the one constantly
attached to Calvin's hip.

510
00:29:42,996 --> 00:29:45,083
Attached? Watch your mouth.

511
00:29:45,156 --> 00:29:47,653
Look at the two of you,
practically joined at the hip.

512
00:29:48,220 --> 00:29:51,523
You're the one who dragged another woman
right to our front door.

513
00:29:51,524 --> 00:29:53,659
Then why don't you bring someone home too?

514
00:29:53,688 --> 00:29:56,261
You think I won't?

515
00:29:56,341 --> 00:29:58,080
Bring Calvin over.

516
00:29:58,081 --> 00:30:00,168
I have a whole line of men waiting for me.

517
00:30:00,169 --> 00:30:01,875
Then go right ahead.

518
00:30:01,900 --> 00:30:04,202
- How dare you!
- That's assault!

519
00:30:04,247 --> 00:30:05,704
And you're having an affair!

520
00:30:05,840 --> 00:30:07,027
Fine, throw that in too!

521
00:30:07,028 --> 00:30:09,441
- You want me to actually hit you?
- I'm calling the police.

522
00:30:11,028 --> 00:30:12,110
Go ahead, hit me!

523
00:30:13,595 --> 00:30:15,001
- Get away from me!
- Hit me!

524
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:16,748
Really?

525
00:30:17,366 --> 00:30:19,366
Both of you caught the cold?

526
00:30:19,851 --> 00:30:22,821
Yes, the wind was pretty harsh yesterday.

527
00:30:23,889 --> 00:30:25,924
Do you think you should see a doctor?

528
00:30:26,379 --> 00:30:27,125
Both of them?

529
00:30:30,028 --> 00:30:31,530
All right.

530
00:30:31,903 --> 00:30:34,800
Don't worry about the shop.
Just get plenty of rest.

531
00:30:37,477 --> 00:30:38,236
The flu?

532
00:30:38,537 --> 00:30:42,355
They both came down
with a bad cold and body aches.

533
00:30:42,861 --> 00:30:45,643
Of all times, they get sick
right after moving in together.

534
00:30:45,777 --> 00:30:50,282
Did Mr. Ji slip something
into Ms. Baek's food?

535
00:30:51,166 --> 00:30:53,884
How can you say something like that
so casually?

536
00:30:55,079 --> 00:30:57,606
I was just joking.

537
00:30:58,023 --> 00:31:00,659
Even as a joke,
there are lines you don't cross.

538
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,315
Understood.

539
00:31:04,563 --> 00:31:05,964
I'll watch what I say.

540
00:31:08,331 --> 00:31:09,234
Calvin.

541
00:31:13,672 --> 00:31:14,539
Hi.

542
00:31:14,775 --> 00:31:15,640
Hello.

543
00:31:15,742 --> 00:31:17,075
What should we do?

544
00:31:17,222 --> 00:31:20,112
Ms. Baek called in sick today.

545
00:31:20,512 --> 00:31:22,881
Mi Young is sick?

546
00:32:10,824 --> 00:32:11,984
Hi, Hee Ju.

547
00:32:14,866 --> 00:32:17,169
Don't worry about it.
You don't have to visit.

548
00:32:23,408 --> 00:32:24,810
Hi, Calvin.

549
00:32:26,044 --> 00:32:28,847
I am running a bit of a fever, though.

550
00:32:30,148 --> 00:32:32,150
Still, nothing to worry about.

551
00:32:33,874 --> 00:32:34,820
Well,

552
00:32:35,620 --> 00:32:37,689
maybe you could drop by for a little bit.

553
00:32:42,227 --> 00:32:45,365
Sure, I'd really appreciate that.

554
00:32:45,697 --> 00:32:46,778
See you soon.

555
00:32:48,533 --> 00:32:50,235
Take care on your way over.

556
00:32:50,725 --> 00:32:51,570
Bye.

557
00:33:03,220 --> 00:33:07,619
(Porridge Day)

558
00:33:10,686 --> 00:33:11,995
You brought flowers?

559
00:33:15,606 --> 00:33:17,061
And is that porridge?

560
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:44,956
Smells great.

561
00:33:47,501 --> 00:33:48,627
It's fine, I'll eat it.

562
00:33:53,765 --> 00:33:56,067
I hate to admit it,
but the guy's got good taste.

563
00:33:58,712 --> 00:34:00,138
Thank you.

564
00:34:04,368 --> 00:34:05,710
Is there anything you're craving?

565
00:34:07,776 --> 00:34:08,912
I'm all right.

566
00:34:09,147 --> 00:34:11,082
No, you need to eat something
to get your energy back.

567
00:34:11,317 --> 00:34:13,451
Hold on, I'll order something.

568
00:34:14,162 --> 00:34:17,020
Don't you want some dessert?

569
00:34:17,389 --> 00:34:18,990
No, I'm good.

570
00:34:19,291 --> 00:34:21,693
Something sweet will perk you right up.

571
00:34:50,855 --> 00:34:53,331
When did you first meet Mr. Ji?

572
00:34:54,058 --> 00:34:55,626
We go back quite a ways.

573
00:34:55,866 --> 00:34:57,067
About eight years.

574
00:34:57,260 --> 00:34:58,330
I see.

575
00:34:58,730 --> 00:34:59,931
What about you?

576
00:35:00,332 --> 00:35:02,339
Longer than the two of you
have known each other.

577
00:35:02,860 --> 00:35:05,971
Were you Ms. Baek's boyfriend?

578
00:35:09,944 --> 00:35:11,142
I see.

579
00:35:11,856 --> 00:35:13,658
No wonder things felt so awkward.

580
00:35:13,945 --> 00:35:16,214
Did we seem awkward?

581
00:35:16,548 --> 00:35:17,642
Ms. Baek and me?

582
00:35:18,350 --> 00:35:21,456
It's just painful watching
your feelings for her...

583
00:35:21,480 --> 00:35:22,887
go entirely unreciprocated.

584
00:35:23,076 --> 00:35:24,222
And what about you?

585
00:35:24,756 --> 00:35:27,158
At this point,
aren't you basically stalking Mr. Ji?

586
00:35:27,905 --> 00:35:29,073
Stalking?

587
00:35:31,329 --> 00:35:32,397
Look who's talking.

588
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:33,658
Excuse me?

589
00:35:34,499 --> 00:35:35,967
I know everything.

590
00:35:36,254 --> 00:35:38,690
I heard you asked Man Joo...

591
00:35:38,771 --> 00:35:40,771
to invite Ms. Baek last time.

592
00:35:42,046 --> 00:35:44,046
At least I'm upfront about it.

593
00:35:44,785 --> 00:35:48,380
I don't pull strings behind people's backs
like you do.

594
00:35:50,791 --> 00:35:51,776
Pull strings?

595
00:35:52,356 --> 00:35:54,352
I'm actually holding back quite a bit.

596
00:35:55,082 --> 00:35:57,141
All I want is for Mi Young...

597
00:35:57,636 --> 00:35:58,936
to be happy.

598
00:36:02,045 --> 00:36:02,932
Well,

599
00:36:03,762 --> 00:36:05,797
I believe love is something
worth fighting for,

600
00:36:06,771 --> 00:36:08,771
but to each their own.

601
00:36:26,651 --> 00:36:29,954
Mr. Ji definitely seems
like the better catch.

602
00:36:30,662 --> 00:36:31,366
What was that?

603
00:36:31,391 --> 00:36:34,192
Mr. Ji is miles ahead of Calvin.

604
00:36:34,358 --> 00:36:36,227
As a partner, in every way.

605
00:36:37,335 --> 00:36:40,732
Isn't that why you moved on
to Mr. Ji in the first place?

606
00:36:41,023 --> 00:36:41,986
Moved on?

607
00:36:42,189 --> 00:36:44,369
Once you get divorced,
you'll move on again.

608
00:36:46,200 --> 00:36:49,040
Personally, I wouldn't recommend Calvin.

609
00:36:50,354 --> 00:36:51,321
He lacks charm.

610
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:56,681
Then what exactly do you find
so appealing about Won Ho?

611
00:36:57,146 --> 00:36:58,622
He's full of charm.

612
00:36:59,356 --> 00:37:00,726
More than I can count.

613
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:03,421
Mr. Ji has...

614
00:37:03,922 --> 00:37:05,922
an endless reservoir of charm.

615
00:37:07,012 --> 00:37:09,394
The more I see him,
the more drawn to him I am.

616
00:37:10,434 --> 00:37:11,358
Take him, then.

617
00:37:12,430 --> 00:37:14,599
Really? You don't mind?

618
00:37:14,925 --> 00:37:16,701
If you can take him off my hands,
be my guest.

619
00:37:16,901 --> 00:37:19,270
I initiated that return a long time ago.

620
00:37:28,680 --> 00:37:30,281
Is that usually your type?

621
00:37:31,335 --> 00:37:32,036
What?

622
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:34,185
She's far too young and shameless.

623
00:37:35,119 --> 00:37:37,086
Spending even a minute with her
is utterly exhausting.

624
00:37:39,232 --> 00:37:40,698
And what about you?

625
00:37:41,359 --> 00:37:43,128
Still set in your old ways, I see.

626
00:37:43,721 --> 00:37:44,388
Meaning?

627
00:37:44,612 --> 00:37:46,297
Is that why you came back?

628
00:37:46,552 --> 00:37:48,318
To reclaim that fixed taste of yours?

629
00:37:48,552 --> 00:37:50,955
Think whatever you want.

630
00:37:52,937 --> 00:37:53,771
Oh, by the way.

631
00:37:56,727 --> 00:37:58,649
Remember that promise I made?

632
00:37:59,650 --> 00:38:00,498
What promise?

633
00:38:01,052 --> 00:38:02,253
Seven years ago.

634
00:38:02,751 --> 00:38:04,751
The one at the street food tent.

635
00:38:06,824 --> 00:38:10,237
I think I might finally keep it soon.

636
00:38:22,777 --> 00:38:27,297
Ha Neul, I'll give you some later,
so stop picking at it.

637
00:38:27,458 --> 00:38:29,007
But I'm starving!

638
00:38:29,129 --> 00:38:33,077
You just ate, and you're already hungry?

639
00:38:36,903 --> 00:38:37,938
Good grief.

640
00:38:39,083 --> 00:38:41,667
Like father, like son.
You got his bottomless appetite.

641
00:38:41,668 --> 00:38:42,754
Unbelievable.

642
00:38:45,152 --> 00:38:47,576
Mom, what is all of this?

643
00:38:47,601 --> 00:38:50,562
I'm dropping it off at Won Ho's.

644
00:38:50,862 --> 00:38:52,664
All of this is for Won Ho?

645
00:38:52,786 --> 00:38:54,899
There's no way
he can finish all that on his own.

646
00:38:55,066 --> 00:38:56,560
Who said it's just for him?

647
00:38:56,586 --> 00:38:57,969
Is he living alone?

648
00:38:58,180 --> 00:38:59,871
Did you make some for his wife too?

649
00:39:00,111 --> 00:39:01,011
What's gotten into you?

650
00:39:01,053 --> 00:39:03,074
This won't even fit in their fridge.

651
00:39:03,204 --> 00:39:04,753
I'll just leave the rest on the balcony.

652
00:39:04,777 --> 00:39:06,744
Are you actually delivering it in person?

653
00:39:06,877 --> 00:39:08,479
Just send it by courier.

654
00:39:08,524 --> 00:39:10,515
Mi Young probably doesn't
even want to see you.

655
00:39:10,631 --> 00:39:11,616
Excuse me?

656
00:39:15,349 --> 00:39:17,722
My mom's food is the best.

657
00:39:17,889 --> 00:39:19,490
At least you have good taste.

658
00:39:19,689 --> 00:39:20,558
Just one more bite.

659
00:39:20,742 --> 00:39:21,693
Hey!

660
00:39:38,843 --> 00:39:40,578
It's getting late.
Aren't you heading home?

661
00:39:41,145 --> 00:39:42,680
I'm not leaving first.

662
00:39:43,781 --> 00:39:45,484
Hee Ju, aren't you going home?

663
00:39:45,783 --> 00:39:47,385
I'll leave when I'm ready.

664
00:40:02,336 --> 00:40:03,330
Hey, Mom.

665
00:40:04,669 --> 00:40:05,837
Yes, we're home. Why?

666
00:40:07,538 --> 00:40:08,239
What?

667
00:40:09,073 --> 00:40:10,863
You're bringing food over now?

668
00:40:12,010 --> 00:40:13,378
Okay, then.

669
00:40:13,643 --> 00:40:14,612
Drive safe.

670
00:40:15,376 --> 00:40:16,180
Okay.

671
00:40:18,816 --> 00:40:21,950
My mother's on her way here now.

672
00:40:22,010 --> 00:40:23,330
Then I'll get going.

673
00:40:23,376 --> 00:40:25,356
Me too.

674
00:40:28,756 --> 00:40:30,361
I should probably get a taxi.

675
00:40:30,650 --> 00:40:31,396
What?

676
00:40:31,996 --> 00:40:33,631
Where are you going at this hour?

677
00:40:33,730 --> 00:40:35,366
To Ah Ri's.

678
00:40:35,463 --> 00:40:37,168
But why now?

679
00:40:37,243 --> 00:40:38,636
Didn't you hear my mom's coming?

680
00:40:39,304 --> 00:40:40,705
That's why I'm going.

681
00:40:40,876 --> 00:40:41,970
Because your mother's coming.

682
00:40:42,183 --> 00:40:44,430
Mom's coming
because she knows you're here.

683
00:40:44,431 --> 00:40:45,977
She's bringing us food.

684
00:40:46,177 --> 00:40:47,271
I'm really sorry, but...

685
00:40:47,351 --> 00:40:50,014
I never asked your mom to bring us food.

686
00:40:50,581 --> 00:40:52,250
I don't even want her food.

687
00:40:53,985 --> 00:40:54,953
Mi Young.

688
00:40:55,271 --> 00:40:57,011
She's still your mother-in-law.

689
00:40:57,137 --> 00:40:59,524
You should at least have
some basic manners.

690
00:41:00,191 --> 00:41:01,626
That's why I'm avoiding her.

691
00:41:01,731 --> 00:41:02,794
To show basic manners.

692
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:05,063
What?

693
00:41:05,463 --> 00:41:07,665
If your mother yanks my hair again,

694
00:41:08,036 --> 00:41:09,634
I'm not letting it slide.

695
00:41:11,375 --> 00:41:12,570
Taxi's here.

696
00:41:13,004 --> 00:41:14,739
I'll be sleeping over at Ah Ri's tonight.

697
00:41:14,970 --> 00:41:16,274
I'm going to go pack a bag.

698
00:41:24,979 --> 00:41:27,552
Alright, time to start on our rebuttal.

699
00:41:28,920 --> 00:41:32,924
They sent over a whole list of reasons
for the divorce.

700
00:41:33,458 --> 00:41:35,193
The rest aside,

701
00:41:36,394 --> 00:41:37,729
this part concerns me.

702
00:41:38,950 --> 00:41:41,943
It says
the relationship really fell apart...

703
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:45,570
after an incident involving violence.

704
00:41:48,539 --> 00:41:51,509
Why did you beat her badly enough
to leave bruises all over her body?

705
00:41:52,076 --> 00:41:53,277
Bruises all over her body?

706
00:41:53,878 --> 00:41:55,113
That's what it says.

707
00:41:56,481 --> 00:41:58,481
"Her body was covered in bruises."

708
00:42:01,371 --> 00:42:02,487
That's not true.

709
00:42:03,785 --> 00:42:04,555
So...

710
00:42:05,125 --> 00:42:07,125
you just stood there,

711
00:42:07,658 --> 00:42:10,228
and somehow your wife
ended up with bruises?

712
00:42:17,705 --> 00:42:20,338
To be exact, I didn't hit her.

713
00:42:21,305 --> 00:42:23,741
I was trying to stop her.
That's why.

714
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:28,846
What was I supposed to do? She was
trying to kill herself with a knife!

715
00:42:28,932 --> 00:42:30,932
I was trying to take the knife away.

716
00:42:31,580 --> 00:42:32,383
That's why.

717
00:42:37,622 --> 00:42:38,589
A knife?

718
00:42:41,893 --> 00:42:44,729
The conflict between the Plaintiff
and the Defendant's mother was not severe.

719
00:42:45,021 --> 00:42:47,031
The Plaintiff also bears
some responsibility for the conflict.

720
00:42:49,554 --> 00:42:50,268
What?

721
00:42:51,169 --> 00:42:53,237
Are we coming home for the holidays?

722
00:42:55,339 --> 00:42:57,608
The Plaintiff rarely called
the Defendant's family,

723
00:42:57,942 --> 00:43:00,144
claiming to be busy with work.

724
00:43:00,645 --> 00:43:03,014
Nevertheless, the Defendant tried to be
understanding of the Plaintiff...

725
00:43:03,331 --> 00:43:05,950
and never once sided with his mother.

726
00:43:05,964 --> 00:43:07,318
No, I'm really sorry.

727
00:43:08,226 --> 00:43:09,654
I don't think we can go.
We're a bit busy.

728
00:43:10,288 --> 00:43:13,057
The Defendant treated the Plaintiff
as more than just a business partner...

729
00:43:13,758 --> 00:43:16,160
and made every effort
to maintain an amicable relationship.

730
00:43:16,578 --> 00:43:17,628
What do you think, Ms. Baek?

731
00:43:17,672 --> 00:43:20,498
The last time I went shopping was
maybe 4 or 5 years ago.

732
00:43:20,638 --> 00:43:22,638
But she shops every week.

733
00:43:23,367 --> 00:43:24,790
The front door always hit
a stack of packages.

734
00:43:28,067 --> 00:43:31,509
Even when the Plaintiff purchased
expensive designer bags beyond her means,

735
00:43:32,043 --> 00:43:34,579
the Defendant tolerated such purchases,
believing them necessary...

736
00:43:35,713 --> 00:43:37,115
for maintaining her professional image
as the CEO.

737
00:43:39,350 --> 00:43:42,687
The Defendant has never assaulted
the Plaintiff.

738
00:43:43,821 --> 00:43:46,290
Instead, the Plaintiff got
heavily drunk from work stress...

739
00:43:46,291 --> 00:43:48,226
and caused a disturbance
with a kitchen knife,

740
00:43:49,692 --> 00:43:51,412
putting the Defendant in danger.

741
00:43:52,063 --> 00:43:53,764
The injuries alleged by the Plaintiff...

742
00:43:54,132 --> 00:43:56,601
occurred unavoidably...

743
00:43:56,868 --> 00:43:58,469
while the Defendant
was attempting to restrain her.

744
00:43:58,790 --> 00:44:00,138
As for sex...

745
00:44:00,139 --> 00:44:02,473
It was the Plaintiff, not the Defendant,

746
00:44:02,743 --> 00:44:04,408
who refused sexual intimacy.

747
00:44:05,343 --> 00:44:08,212
The Plaintiff first suggested sleeping
in separate rooms.

748
00:44:09,768 --> 00:44:12,049
As both parties became busy with work,

749
00:44:12,717 --> 00:44:14,919
they naturally grew apart.

750
00:44:15,993 --> 00:44:18,047
Therefore, the Defendant cannot be held
solely responsible.

751
00:44:19,049 --> 00:44:21,419
The Defendant is making efforts
to repair the relationship.

752
00:44:22,486 --> 00:44:25,329
The Defendant does not wish
to end the marriage.

753
00:44:25,997 --> 00:44:28,266
He sincerely hopes the Plaintiff will...

754
00:44:29,534 --> 00:44:33,304
make a more active effort
to restore their marital relationship.

755
00:44:33,971 --> 00:44:35,573
Is he serious?

756
00:44:35,940 --> 00:44:38,609
How can he say this with a straight face?

757
00:44:39,010 --> 00:44:41,445
After the way he treated me
our entire marriage!

758
00:44:41,945 --> 00:44:44,618
That's how people usually frame things
in these documents.

759
00:44:44,978 --> 00:44:46,038
Like I said,

760
00:44:46,091 --> 00:44:48,186
that's not your husband talking.

761
00:44:51,031 --> 00:44:53,124
That's his attorney doing
what he does best.

762
00:44:54,098 --> 00:44:55,638
Forget everything else.

763
00:44:56,211 --> 00:44:57,195
This part right here.

764
00:44:57,495 --> 00:45:00,331
The part about me causing a scene
with a kitchen knife.

765
00:45:03,768 --> 00:45:05,469
Yes, I was the one who caused the scene,

766
00:45:06,583 --> 00:45:08,418
but I was also the only one...

767
00:45:09,006 --> 00:45:10,308
who got hurt because of it.

768
00:45:13,144 --> 00:45:13,945
Is that so?

769
00:45:14,979 --> 00:45:17,281
Then, could you tell me...

770
00:45:17,852 --> 00:45:20,184
a little more about that part?

771
00:45:27,792 --> 00:45:28,859
That day,

772
00:45:32,296 --> 00:45:33,331
for a very long time,

773
00:45:35,466 --> 00:45:36,334
I was passed out...

774
00:45:37,969 --> 00:45:40,004
on the floor all by myself.

775
00:45:45,884 --> 00:45:47,011
He left me there...

776
00:45:48,846 --> 00:45:50,846
on that cold floor.

777
00:45:56,387 --> 00:45:57,521
That day,

778
00:45:58,623 --> 00:46:00,091
he abandoned me again.

779
00:46:04,533 --> 00:46:07,598
When I was at my most vulnerable.

780
00:46:25,516 --> 00:46:28,185
I had to hurry and come see Mr. Kwon.

781
00:46:28,919 --> 00:46:30,655
Go wash up
and make sure you eat something.

782
00:46:48,606 --> 00:46:51,342
Twice. For the exact same reason.

783
00:47:03,654 --> 00:47:04,609
That's more than enough.

784
00:47:06,757 --> 00:47:07,892
I think we're going to...

785
00:47:08,273 --> 00:47:09,126
win.

786
00:47:18,158 --> 00:47:20,204
Welcome.

787
00:47:20,865 --> 00:47:22,006
Please come in.

788
00:47:22,007 --> 00:47:23,406
This way, please.

789
00:47:23,918 --> 00:47:24,842
Hello.

790
00:47:26,478 --> 00:47:29,380
I made sure you got it.

791
00:47:29,465 --> 00:47:31,449
With an off-the-shoulder wedding dress.

792
00:47:31,585 --> 00:47:32,891
I see.

793
00:48:06,185 --> 00:48:09,453
Wow, it's so crowded.

794
00:48:10,218 --> 00:48:13,457
I think each couple has at least 5
or 6 family members with them.

795
00:48:13,824 --> 00:48:16,018
Sons-in-law, daughters-in-law,
and grandkids too.

796
00:48:16,624 --> 00:48:19,196
Some even brought the other in-laws!

797
00:48:19,463 --> 00:48:23,200
This isn't a wedding.
It's a full-on festival!

798
00:48:23,934 --> 00:48:24,835
I agree.

799
00:48:25,169 --> 00:48:28,128
If we'd known,
we would've prepared a whole feast!

800
00:48:28,215 --> 00:48:29,373
Maybe we should've!

801
00:48:35,221 --> 00:48:37,048
You look amazing!

802
00:48:57,131 --> 00:48:58,402
Hey there.

803
00:48:59,103 --> 00:49:01,539
I could tell you put a lot of work
into this.

804
00:49:01,952 --> 00:49:02,862
A true professional.

805
00:49:03,082 --> 00:49:04,108
Of course.

806
00:49:05,556 --> 00:49:07,711
Are you feeling better?

807
00:49:08,679 --> 00:49:09,447
Yes.

808
00:49:13,053 --> 00:49:14,852
I think you have a slight fever.

809
00:49:15,686 --> 00:49:17,054
I'm fine.

810
00:49:17,474 --> 00:49:18,842
Don't push yourself too much.

811
00:49:20,024 --> 00:49:21,358
Have this when you need a little boost.

812
00:49:23,340 --> 00:49:24,195
Thanks.

813
00:49:41,579 --> 00:49:42,813
Shall we?

814
00:49:43,633 --> 00:49:44,334
Yes.

815
00:49:51,845 --> 00:49:54,859
You look great!
Try getting a little closer.

816
00:49:54,985 --> 00:49:56,660
All right.

817
00:50:05,963 --> 00:50:06,904
Hey.

818
00:50:07,605 --> 00:50:08,572
What do you think?

819
00:50:08,939 --> 00:50:10,975
Doesn't this make you want
to get married too?

820
00:50:11,109 --> 00:50:12,176
Why, you little!

821
00:50:21,886 --> 00:50:23,220
Keep smiling!

822
00:50:23,699 --> 00:50:26,790
It's nice seeing you
somewhere like this for a change.

823
00:50:27,091 --> 00:50:29,012
I'm used to seeing brides,
not the priest officiating!

824
00:50:29,092 --> 00:50:29,793
So,

825
00:50:30,194 --> 00:50:33,099
where would you rank me
among today's brides?

826
00:50:34,164 --> 00:50:35,666
Not at the bottom, at least.

827
00:50:38,702 --> 00:50:40,582
My buddy said he was renewing his vows,

828
00:50:40,583 --> 00:50:43,274
so I figured I'd come check it out
and see you while I was here.

829
00:50:43,922 --> 00:50:45,296
Seeing it all,
I actually felt pretty proud.

830
00:50:46,510 --> 00:50:48,145
Honestly, at our age,

831
00:50:48,612 --> 00:50:50,185
you never think you'd get to wear
a wedding dress again.

832
00:50:50,814 --> 00:50:52,909
What you're doing is really amazing.

833
00:50:54,365 --> 00:50:55,786
It's not like I'm doing charity work.

834
00:50:56,703 --> 00:50:58,022
A lot of seniors at our center...

835
00:50:58,956 --> 00:51:01,325
never got to have a proper wedding.

836
00:51:01,638 --> 00:51:02,526
Really?

837
00:51:02,960 --> 00:51:04,960
They still haven't had a wedding?

838
00:51:05,147 --> 00:51:05,996
So many of them.

839
00:51:06,430 --> 00:51:09,099
Not everyone gets to experience
something like this.

840
00:51:09,600 --> 00:51:11,035
Then let me arrange one for them!

841
00:51:11,298 --> 00:51:11,902
What?

842
00:51:12,043 --> 00:51:14,043
I'll give the seniors at your center...

843
00:51:14,263 --> 00:51:15,372
the wedding they never had.

844
00:51:16,273 --> 00:51:19,143
What's with that all of a sudden?

845
00:51:19,410 --> 00:51:20,544
Are you doing charity again?

846
00:51:21,111 --> 00:51:23,111
Well, not exactly.

847
00:51:23,257 --> 00:51:25,437
I've never done charity like this before.

848
00:51:25,590 --> 00:51:27,084
Are you kidding me?

849
00:51:27,223 --> 00:51:28,335
Do you even think?

850
00:51:28,528 --> 00:51:30,440
Today's the first day of the event!

851
00:51:30,441 --> 00:51:32,995
Did you really have to bring
this up right now? Can't you see I'm busy?

852
00:51:33,791 --> 00:51:35,148
I know that, but...

853
00:51:35,288 --> 00:51:36,894
I was talking with Mr. Kwon about it.

854
00:51:36,961 --> 00:51:39,296
So I thought I'd tell you before I forget.

855
00:51:39,803 --> 00:51:40,531
What?

856
00:51:41,432 --> 00:51:42,399
With who?

857
00:51:42,866 --> 00:51:44,866
Mr. Kwon came by earlier.

858
00:51:45,506 --> 00:51:47,271
To support his friend's wedding.

859
00:51:50,526 --> 00:51:51,508
Ji Won Ho.

860
00:51:52,026 --> 00:51:54,678
You're impossible.

861
00:51:56,480 --> 00:52:01,051
Did you forget why we're exchanging
divorce papers in the first place?

862
00:52:02,426 --> 00:52:04,388
It's all because of that precious Mr. Kwon
of yours.

863
00:52:04,519 --> 00:52:06,790
He's the reason Dal Rae ended
up like that!

864
00:52:06,819 --> 00:52:08,058
Watch what you say.

865
00:52:08,712 --> 00:52:11,086
Don't blame Mr. Kwon for that.
That's on you and me.

866
00:52:12,546 --> 00:52:14,252
You need to break that nasty habit...

867
00:52:14,253 --> 00:52:17,101
of bringing up the past
and blaming everyone else!

868
00:52:23,941 --> 00:52:26,810
You need to shut your damn mouth.

869
00:52:56,753 --> 00:52:57,608
Mi Young.

870
00:53:02,046 --> 00:53:03,247
It's been a while.

871
00:53:06,050 --> 00:53:09,853
I didn't mean to eavesdrop, but I heard
you and Won Ho talking earlier.

872
00:53:11,455 --> 00:53:12,623
About what happened that day,

873
00:53:13,590 --> 00:53:14,925
I'm truly sorry.

874
00:53:17,795 --> 00:53:19,329
If you were really sorry,

875
00:53:21,398 --> 00:53:22,866
you wouldn't be doing this.

876
00:53:25,703 --> 00:53:29,473
It hurts just to see you.

877
00:53:31,434 --> 00:53:32,443
I understand.

878
00:53:34,099 --> 00:53:36,447
Well, then, goodbye.

879
00:53:37,865 --> 00:53:39,349
Won Ho was in pain too.

880
00:53:42,499 --> 00:53:44,499
Won Ho was hurting...

881
00:53:45,322 --> 00:53:46,323
for just as long as you were.

882
00:53:46,539 --> 00:53:48,425
Hurt over what?

883
00:53:49,393 --> 00:53:51,061
The truth is, that day...

884
00:55:06,880 --> 00:55:08,939
I'm never bringing up charity ever again.

885
00:55:34,822 --> 00:55:35,599
We...

886
00:55:38,202 --> 00:55:39,369
need to talk.

887
00:55:39,770 --> 00:55:40,671
What now?

888
00:55:40,850 --> 00:55:42,850
Are you going to hit
my other cheek this time?

889
00:55:44,274 --> 00:55:45,342
I just had a talk...

890
00:55:48,245 --> 00:55:50,681
with Mr. Kwon.

891
00:55:55,463 --> 00:55:57,688
About what?

892
00:56:00,123 --> 00:56:01,525
About what happened that day.

893
00:56:08,628 --> 00:56:11,515
I don't care what Mr. Kwon asked
you to do!

894
00:56:11,541 --> 00:56:13,337
Can't you see the work piled up here?

895
00:56:13,604 --> 00:56:15,839
Even with both of us,
we're cutting it close.

896
00:56:16,173 --> 00:56:19,810
Are you seriously going to leave
all this to me and go?

897
00:56:20,577 --> 00:56:22,980
I know it's too much for you alone,

898
00:56:23,280 --> 00:56:26,750
but Mr. Kwon is like a father to me.

899
00:56:27,317 --> 00:56:29,253
How am I supposed to turn him down?

900
00:56:30,137 --> 00:56:31,088
I heard...

901
00:56:32,256 --> 00:56:34,256
you were trying to come back
to me that day.

902
00:56:40,364 --> 00:56:42,364
Yes, Mr. Kwon. I'm on my way.

903
00:56:42,642 --> 00:56:43,867
But the thing is,

904
00:56:44,155 --> 00:56:47,537
I'm worried about Mi Young.
I think I'll have to go back.

905
00:56:47,871 --> 00:56:49,740
But I'll send a friend
over right away instead.

906
00:56:49,839 --> 00:56:50,908
I'm really sorry, Mr. Kwon.

907
00:56:51,353 --> 00:56:52,509
I'll call you later.

908
00:57:05,377 --> 00:57:07,524
- Are you trying to kill someone?
- Are you okay?

909
00:57:08,125 --> 00:57:10,527
I'm clearly not okay!
Do I look okay to you?

910
00:57:10,528 --> 00:57:13,030
You should call
the insurance company right away.

911
00:57:13,031 --> 00:57:14,204
I'm running late, so...

912
00:57:14,205 --> 00:57:15,632
I'm just as busy!

913
00:57:20,164 --> 00:57:22,904
Forget the illegal U-turn.
I think he's drunk!

914
00:57:22,911 --> 00:57:24,251
Come talk to him!

915
00:57:24,252 --> 00:57:25,585
Give me one second.
Let me make a quick call.

916
00:57:25,586 --> 00:57:26,710
He was definitely drinking.

917
00:57:37,589 --> 00:57:39,423
What are you talking about?

918
00:57:39,790 --> 00:57:41,325
Why are you bringing that up right now?

919
00:57:42,893 --> 00:57:43,794
And...

920
00:57:46,939 --> 00:57:48,939
the day I tried to kill myself.

921
00:57:52,939 --> 00:57:53,870
Even then,

922
00:57:55,931 --> 00:57:57,939
you never abandoned me.

923
00:57:59,710 --> 00:58:01,377
I begged you to stay.

924
00:58:01,945 --> 00:58:04,147
I told you I couldn't do it alone.

925
00:58:05,247 --> 00:58:06,650
I begged you not to go.

926
00:58:07,305 --> 00:58:10,387
I told you I couldn't do it by myself!

927
00:58:10,921 --> 00:58:13,256
I know. I'm sorry about everything.

928
00:58:13,495 --> 00:58:14,925
It's all my fault.

929
00:58:15,759 --> 00:58:17,759
Everything's a mess now.

930
00:58:19,006 --> 00:58:20,564
Mom and Dad are gone...

931
00:58:21,268 --> 00:58:22,499
and so is Dal Rae.

932
00:58:23,667 --> 00:58:25,769
I couldn't even protect my own child.

933
00:58:26,728 --> 00:58:29,773
I want to die with them.

934
00:58:30,807 --> 00:58:32,776
Let me go with them.

935
00:58:32,802 --> 00:58:34,696
That's not true. Why would you think that?

936
00:58:34,711 --> 00:58:36,313
Don't say that, Mi Young.

937
00:58:36,613 --> 00:58:38,248
Let go!

938
00:58:42,367 --> 00:58:43,353
Stay back.

939
00:58:43,387 --> 00:58:46,556
I'm going to die too.

940
00:58:46,654 --> 00:58:48,725
Mi Young, put that down.

941
00:58:49,051 --> 00:58:49,926
Put it down.

942
00:58:49,927 --> 00:58:52,353
Stay back.

943
00:58:52,354 --> 00:58:53,597
- Put it down.
- No.

944
00:58:55,107 --> 00:58:56,233
Let go of me!

945
00:58:57,540 --> 00:58:58,435
Let go! Stop!

946
00:59:01,993 --> 00:59:03,573
Snap out of it!

947
00:59:03,574 --> 00:59:07,177
Don't touch me! Stop it!

948
00:59:09,346 --> 00:59:10,914
The person who almost died that day...

949
00:59:12,749 --> 00:59:13,884
wasn't me.

950
00:59:36,727 --> 00:59:38,742
I want to die too.

951
00:59:45,625 --> 00:59:48,051
I want to die.

952
00:59:53,058 --> 00:59:54,257
You're the one...

953
00:59:57,043 --> 00:59:58,028
who got stabbed.

954
00:59:59,663 --> 01:00:02,032
What are you even saying?
I need to work. Get out.

955
01:00:05,249 --> 01:00:06,436
Wait, Mi Young.

956
01:00:06,670 --> 01:00:07,896
Wait.

957
01:00:07,916 --> 01:00:08,905
Mi Young.

958
01:00:26,656 --> 01:00:27,791
It wasn't you.

959
01:00:29,826 --> 01:00:30,861
It was me.

960
01:00:36,372 --> 01:00:38,668
I'm the one who put you in danger.

961
01:00:41,124 --> 01:00:41,972
I almost...

962
01:00:43,166 --> 01:00:45,199
I almost killed you.

963
01:00:47,310 --> 01:00:49,079
I'm sorry.

964
01:00:50,213 --> 01:00:51,448
I'm so sorry.

965
01:00:52,449 --> 01:00:53,984
I'm sorry.

966
01:01:24,990 --> 01:01:27,964
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

967
01:01:28,635 --> 01:01:29,819
Play dumb?

968
01:01:30,086 --> 01:01:31,788
Do you really think this feels natural?

969
01:01:31,881 --> 01:01:32,889
Let's just do it, baby.

970
01:01:33,088 --> 01:01:34,858
"Let's do it, baby?"

971
01:01:34,928 --> 01:01:36,059
What's up with her?

972
01:01:36,275 --> 01:01:38,115
You're being overly nice to Won Ho,

973
01:01:38,116 --> 01:01:40,155
so he's trying to leave
because he's uncomfortable.

974
01:01:40,156 --> 01:01:40,922
Some kind of strategy?

975
01:01:41,656 --> 01:01:44,100
Just act like you used to!

976
01:01:44,434 --> 01:01:46,269
You don't know when to stop.

977
01:01:46,270 --> 01:01:47,904
You're stubborn as a leech!

978
01:01:47,905 --> 01:01:50,090
Sure, okay! But you're just as stubborn!

979
01:01:50,091 --> 01:01:52,542
Are you trying to ruin our family?

980
01:01:52,764 --> 01:01:54,936
My son isn't crazy enough to date
a whore like you!

981
01:01:54,937 --> 01:01:56,346
You know what? I am crazy!

982
01:01:56,357 --> 01:01:58,648
I happen to be Hee Ju's...

983
01:01:59,676 --> 01:02:00,777
boyfriend.
